    refactor(cleanup): behavior-preserving cleanup debt reduction (C01-C10)
    
    Remove disconnected and duplicated machinery without changing supported
    behavior:
    
    - C01: drop unused Portify monitor helpers (EventRecord, EventLogger,
      classify_failure, generate_diagnostic_report); requirement assertions
      migrated to live ExecutionLog/DiagnosticsCollector/executor owners.
    - C02: retire the orphan scripts/publish.sh wrapper; correct publishing docs.
    - C03: share identical recipe primitives via swarm/recipes/_primitives.py;
      recipe exports, clocks, defaults and caps unchanged.
    - C04: retire unwired Portify failure helpers (get_failure_handler_name,
      handle_non_writable_output, handle_missing_skills); registry unchanged.
    - C05: remove inactive setup.py and MANIFEST.in (Hatchling payload unchanged).
    - C06: share validation text helpers via pipeline/validation_text.py.
    - C07: share the normalize/reduce atomic byte writer via swarm/atomic.py.
    - C08: drop the Black dev dependency and [tool.black]; Ruff stays pinned.
    - C09: registered-None recipes resolve to the concrete Passthrough.
    - C10: drop the roadmap apply_decomposition_pass wrapper; tests retarget
      decompose_deliverables.
    
    Adds characterization, migration and installed-resource tests. Full suite:
    no new failures versus baseline.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

